# Keep every text file at LF on every platform.
#
# This tree ships artifacts whose bytes are compared against recorded digests, and
# some of the files that describe or verify them are hashed as well --
# requirements-desktop-windows.lock is digested into the build SBOM. A Windows
# checkout with core.autocrlf must not silently rewrite line endings in any of
# them, and pip-compile on Windows produced that lock with CRLF, so the rule also
# normalises the file back to the LF form the rest of the repository uses.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Not text, whatever a heuristic decides: vendor/libusb-COPYING is compared byte
# for byte against the copy inside the pinned libusb source archive.
vendor/libusb-COPYING -text
*.dll binary
*.dylib binary
*.whl binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.tar.bz2 binary
*.icns binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
